Carafe: the orchestrator reads the registered threads with their load and places them on cores.
wine_nx_thread_views gives each thread's share of a core since the last call, its core mask and whether it may
be moved (not pinned by the program, not a graphics helper on core 3, not a shader worker). wine_nx_thread_place
moves a Wine thread and its server connection thread to the given cores. wine_nx_thread_reserve_core keeps shader
workers off one core, now and when they next compile, so the main thread can have that core to itself.
wine_nx_thread_tid names the registered thread behind a Horizon handle, for the profiler's wait counts.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

